.TH GHDEB 1 "2026-08-03" "ghdeb 0.7.49" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ghdeb \- Install .deb packages from GitHub Releases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ghdeb
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ghdeb
manages .deb packages downloaded from GitHub Releases. It handles
architecture detection, asset matching, downloading, and installation.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS install
.B ghdeb install
.IB owner / repo [ @tag ]
.br
.B ghdeb install
.I shortname
.PP
Install or upgrade a package to the specified version. If no tag is given,
the latest stable release is used. Short names from the catalog are also
supported (e.g.,
.IR bat ,
.IR fd ).
.SS upgrade
.B ghdeb upgrade
.RI [ owner/repo ]
.PP
Upgrade managed packages. If no package is specified, all managed packages
are upgraded. Automatically scans for orphan packages before upgrading.
.SS reinstall
.B ghdeb reinstall
.I pkg
.PP
Force reinstall a package by downloading and installing the latest release
again. The history entry is marked as a reinstall.
.SS search
.B ghdeb search
.I pattern
.PP
Search the package catalog by name, pretty name, or summary. Supports
regular expressions.
.SS update
.B ghdeb update
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.PP
With
.BR \-\-verbose ,
print detailed background steps (catalog load, per-package check with cache hit
or fetched version, asset validation, snapshot assembly) instead of the compact
progress bar.
.PP
Similar to
.B apt update
. Queries the latest version from GitHub and the locally installed version for
each catalog entry, determines whether it is upgradeable, validates and removes
catalog entries without a .deb package for the current architecture, and writes
the results to a single system cache file (/var/cache/ghdeb/cache.json). Like
.B apt update
, this writes to the root-owned system cache and may prompt for
.BR sudo .
After this,
.B ghdeb list
reads only that snapshot and does not query the network.
.SS list
.B ghdeb list
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
List all catalog entries, reading only the local snapshot produced by
.B ghdeb update
without hitting the network. Shows short name, repo, installed version, and the
latest version. Entries whose installed version is older than the latest are
flagged as upgradeable. Version columns show "-" when update has not been run.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output the list as JSON.

.SS catalog
.B ghdeb catalog
.I subcommand
.PP
Manage the package catalog. The catalog maps short names to GitHub
repositories (or direct .deb URLs) and is used for short-name installs.
.RS
.B ghdeb list
List all catalog entries.
.TP
.B ghdeb catalog show
.I name
Show detailed information about a catalog entry.
.TP
.B ghdeb catalog search
.I pattern
Search the catalog (same as the top-level
.B search
command).
.TP
.B ghdeb catalog add
.I name
.B \-\-repo
.I owner/repo
.RB [ \-\-url
.I deb-url ]
.RB [ \-\-pretty-name
.I name ]
.RB [ \-\-website
.I url ]
.RB [ \-\-summary
.I text ]
.RB [ \-\-gpg-key
.I url ]
Add an entry to the system catalog
.RI ( /etc/ghdeb/catalog.toml ).
At least one of
.B \-\-repo
or
.B \-\-url
is required. If
.B \-\-url
is given, the package can be installed from a direct .deb download URL
(non-GitHub source). The
.B \-\-gpg-key
option specifies a URL to a GPG public key for signature verification.
.TP
.B ghdeb catalog delete
.I name
Remove an entry from the system catalog.
.TP
.TP
.B ghdeb catalog modify
.I name
.B \-\-repo
.I owner/repo
Modify the repository associated with an existing system catalog entry.
.TP
.B ghdeb catalog validate
.RB [ name ]
.RB [ \-\-all ]
Validate catalog entries and remove those that provide no .deb for the
current architecture. Without arguments, validate all entries; with a
name, validate only that entry.
.RE
.SS show / info
.B ghdeb show
.I pkg
.PP
Show the latest release information for a package, including matched
download assets for the current architecture.
.B info
is an alias for
.BR show .
.SS history
.B ghdeb history
.IB owner / repo
.PP
Show the complete operation history (install, upgrade, purge) for a package.
.SS purge
.B ghdeb purge
.I pkg
.PP
Uninstall a package using
.B apt-get purge
and clean up dependencies with
.BR autoremove .
The ghdeb management record is also removed.
.SS clean
.B ghdeb clean
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.PP
Remove cached .deb files from
.BR /var/cache/ghdeb/ .
Use
.B \-\-dry\-run
to preview what would be deleted without actually removing files.
.SS version
.B ghdeb version
.PP
Print the ghdeb version.
.SH CATALOG
The package catalog is stored in TOML format at the system path
.B /etc/ghdeb/catalog.toml
and ships with a curated list of known GitHub .deb packages.
.PP
Catalog entry format:
.EX
[bat]
repo = "sharkdp/bat"
pretty_name = "bat"
website = "https://github.com/sharkdp/bat"
summary = "A cat(1) clone with syntax highlighting"
.EE
.PP
For non-GitHub sources, a direct URL template can be specified:
.EX
[myapp]
url = "https://example.com/releases/myapp_{version}_{arch}.deb"
pretty_name = "My App"
summary = "My custom application"
.EE
.PP
URL placeholders:
.B {version}
(release tag without leading v),
.B {arch}
(dpkg architecture name).
.SH GPG VERIFICATION
When a catalog entry includes a
.B gpg_key
field, ghdeb will attempt to verify the .deb package signature after
download using the specified GPG public key. If verification fails, the
installation is aborted.
.SH CACHE
.B ghdeb
caches each catalog package's state (installed, installed version, GitHub
latest version, upgradeable) in a single flattened
.B /var/cache/ghdeb/cache.json
with a 24-hour TTL. Downloaded .deb files are cached in
.BR /var/cache/ghdeb/ .
.SH STATE
Managed package records are stored in
.BR /var/cache/ghdeb/history.json .
.SH LOCALE
Output language is determined by the
.B LANG
environment variable. Chinese (zh_*) produces Chinese output; all other
locales produce English output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/ghdeb/catalog.toml
System package catalog (curated list of known GitHub .deb packages).
.TP
.B /var/cache/ghdeb/cache.json
Unified flattened cache: one record per catalog package (installed state,
installed/latest versions, upgradeable; 24h TTL).
.TP
.B /var/cache/ghdeb/*.deb
Downloaded .deb package cache.
.TP
.B /var/cache/ghdeb/history.json
Managed package state records.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (invalid arguments, network failure, install failure, etc.).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ghdeb install bat
Install bat using its catalog short name.
.TP
.B ghdeb install LeisureLinux/ghdeb
Install the latest version of ghdeb.
.TP
.B ghdeb install LeisureLinux/ghdeb@v0.7.49
Install a specific version of ghdeb.
.TP
.B ghdeb update
Refresh latest/installed version info into local snapshot.
.TP
.B ghdeb upgrade
Upgrade all managed packages.
.TP
.B ghdeb search monitor
Search the catalog for packages matching "monitor".
.TP
.B ghdeb list
List all catalog entries.
.TP
.B ghdeb catalog add myapp \-\-repo user/myapp \-\-summary "My app"
Add a custom entry to the system catalog.
.TP
.B ghdeb catalog add myapp \-\-url "https://example.com/myapp_{version}_{arch}.deb"
Add a non-GitHub source to the catalog.
.TP
.B ghdeb catalog delete myapp
Remove a custom entry from the system catalog.
.TP
.B ghdeb clean \-\-dry\-run
Preview cached files that would be cleaned.
.TP
.B ghdeb purge rustdesk
Uninstall rustdesk and clean up.
.SH SHELL COMPLETION
.B ghdeb
provides shell completion scripts for bash, zsh, and fish. After installation,
completions are automatically available for new shells. For existing shells:
.PP
.B bash:
source /usr/share/bash-completion/completions/ghdeb
.br
or restart your shell.
.PP
.B zsh:
run
.I compinit
or restart your shell. Completions are installed to
.IR /usr/share/zsh/site-functions/_ghdeb .
.PP
.B fish:
Completions are installed to
.IR /usr/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/ghdeb.fish .
